\ A raise inside a prelude compound reached from a compiled user word. Under eager the chain
\ crosses the compiled/interpreted boundary at `print-line`, and the `say` row is contributed
\ by compiled `report` during the unwind. No flags: one golden binds the interpreted and eager
\ suites, which is the pin that neither tier drops the row. The interpreted twin with the
\ eager drop documented is error_frames_cross_file.1z, still pinned `--compile=off` until the
\ golden-convergence pass retires that fork.

say: ( v -- ) [ print-line 0 drop ] ;
report: ( v -- ) [ say 0 drop ] ;

42 report
